**`cache.put` failure aborts an already-successful fetch.**

If `cache.put` rejects (e.g. `QuotaExceededError` when caching large `.wasm`/`.rten` binaries), the exception propagates out of `cacheFirst`, causing `event.respondWith` to reject even though a valid `response` was already fetched from the network. The user gets a failed request instead of the content that was actually retrieved.

